  "sculpt": {
    "_about": "THE GIRAFFE (2026-11-05, 2nd pass: a longer head with its boss, thick tufted ossicones, the patches down to the knees and hocks and on the jaw, a dark brush of a mane, the long tail with its black tassel, broad hooves): a short trunk falling steeply from high withers and massive shoulders to the rump, the belly tucked; the neck thick out of the shoulders and tapering to a slim throat, a short upright dark mane along it; a long tapering head, the median ossicone's boss on the brow, long mobile lips, ears out sideways under the kept ossicones; long slim legs, the forearm and gaskin patched, knobby knees and hocks, plain pale cannons to two-toed hooves; the coat the giraffe network (spots) on a pale ground, liver patches (2026-11-08) The EARS are `fin` sheets (sharp.js): leaf-shaped, cupped, the base buried in an earBase fillet.",
